======================================================================================================================
K2 (exact-relations compute) -- the deep-MOND expansion as a Bernoulli series; is c2 = 1/2 measurable?
======================================================================================================================

  (A) THE SERIES.  s/(1-e^{-s}) = sum B_n^+ s^n/n!  (Bernoulli numbers, B_1 = +1/2).
      n :  0      1      2      3      4      5      6
      B_n^+/n! : +1.000000  +0.500000  +0.083333  +0.000000  -0.001389  +0.000000  +0.000033
      so  g_obs/a_0 = s + 0.500000 s^2 + 0.083333 s^3 + 0.000000 s^4 + -0.001389 s^5 + ...
  [PASS] c2 (the g_bar coefficient) is exactly 1/2   (0.5)
  [PASS] c3 (the g_bar^{3/2} coefficient) is exactly 1/12   (0.08333333333333333)
  [PASS] c4 (the g_bar^2 coefficient) is exactly 0   (0.0)
  [PASS] c5 is exactly -1/720   (-0.001388888888888889)
  [PASS] series to s^9 matches the kernel at s=0.05 to its own truncation bound   (error -2.22e-16, truncation bound 2.04e-21)
  [PASS] series to s^9 matches the kernel at s=0.2 to its own truncation bound   (error -2.00e-15, truncation bound 2.14e-15)
  [PASS] series to s^9 matches the kernel at s=0.5 to its own truncation bound   (error -2.03e-11, truncation bound 2.05e-11)
  [PASS] series to s^9 matches the kernel at s=1.0 to its own truncation bound   (error -2.04e-08, truncation bound 2.14e-08)
  [PASS] series to s^9 matches the kernel at s=2.0 to its own truncation bound   (error -1.94e-05, truncation bound 2.35e-05)

      the same expansion for four interpolating functions -- c2 is the family discriminator:
        Route A   1/(1-exp(-sqrt y))           c2 =  0.5000   c3 =  0.0833
        MOND 'simple'  (1+sqrt(1+4/y))/2       c2 =  0.5000   c3 =  0.1250
        MOND 'standard'                        c2 = -0.0000   c3 =  0.2500
        alpha=1  sqrt(1+1/y)   (E0/E3)         c2 =  0.0000   c3 =  0.5000
      -> c2 = 1/2 for the sqrt(y)-expansion family (Route A, simple); c2 = 0 for the integer-y family
         (standard, alpha=1).  CREDIT, against interest: this split is the published 'simple beats
         standard' result -- Famaey & Binney 2005 (MNRAS 363, 603), Zhao & Famaey 2006 -- decided the
         same way from the Milky Way terminal curve.  The Bernoulli identification is new; the
         empirical content of c2 != 0 is not.

  (B) RESTATEMENT TEST -- executed.  Derive the candidate from v^4 = G M_b a_0 plus algebra.
      v^4 = G M_b a_0  <=>  g_obs^2 = a_0 g_bar  <=>  g_obs/a_0 = s, EXACTLY and with no further terms.
      So the LEADING term IS the BTFR -- that half is a restatement and is labelled one.  The BTFR
      predicts a pure power law, i.e. c2 = c3 = 0; every coefficient beyond the first is content it
      does not have.  The candidate's content is therefore exactly the residual g_obs - sqrt(a_0 g_bar).
      Corollary the proposer flagged and which is worth recording: eliminating a_0 between two radii,
        ln f_DM(r1)/ln f_DM(r2) = sqrt(g_bar(r1)/g_bar(r2)),
      is a_0-FREE, so it fails criterion (2) by construction.  Verified numerically:
        a_0 = 7.000e-11:  ln f1/ln f2 = 3.162278   sqrt(g1/g2) = 3.162278   (identical, a_0 cancelled)
        a_0 = 9.360e-11:  ln f1/ln f2 = 3.162278   sqrt(g1/g2) = 3.162278   (identical, a_0 cancelled)
        a_0 = 1.130e-10:  ln f1/ln f2 = 3.162278   sqrt(g1/g2) = 3.162278   (identical, a_0 cancelled)
        a_0 = 3.000e-10:  ln f1/ln f2 = 3.162278   sqrt(g1/g2) = 3.162278   (identical, a_0 cancelled)
  [PASS] the a_0-free corollary is genuinely a_0-free (holds at every a_0)   (the ratio does not move when a_0 moves by 4x)
  [PASS] is_restatement of v^4 = G M_b a_0 for the LEADING term (labelled, not hidden)   (TRUE for the s^1 term; FALSE for c2, which the BTFR sets to 0)

  (C) SPARC.  c2 is read four ways, because the answer depends on how it is read.
      A  the propose-stage design: Y = g_obs/a_0 - s regressed on [s^2, s^3], UNWEIGHTED
      B  the ratio design:  r = g_obs/sqrt(a_0 g_bar) = 1 + c2 s + c3 s^2, UNWEIGHTED
      C  the ratio design, WEIGHTED by velocity errors PLUS an intrinsic scatter set so chi2/dof = 1
      D  design C with a fixed 3-sigma clip applied twice (declared in advance, not tuned)
      All four are the SAME statement about the SAME points.  Any spread between them is estimator
      systematic and must be carried on the number.

