======================================================================================================================
  VERDICT ON K2
======================================================================================================================
  (1) measured quantities?  YES -- g_obs and g_bar, per point.
  (2) a_0 with a PREDICTED coefficient?  NO.  c2 = 1/2 is a pure number with no a_0 in it; a_0 enters
      only as the variable the expansion is taken in.  The sharp claim fails criterion (2).
  (3) RAR-class scatter?  the estimator systematic alone spans 2.501 in c2 across
      four fits of the same statement to the same points -- comparable to the 0.5 signal.
  (4) unstated?  the Bernoulli identification is new; the empirical content (c2 != 0, i.e. the
      sqrt(y)-expansion family beats the integer-y family) is Famaey & Binney 2005 / Zhao & Famaey 2006.
  (5) restatement?  the LEADING term IS v^4 = G M_b a_0 -- labelled TRUE for that half.  c2 is not.
  CORRECTION TO THE PROPOSE-STAGE HEADLINE, stated explicitly:  its design (A here) gives the same
  central value, c2 = +0.840, but its quoted +-0.117 was a POINT-level error on 1979 points that
  cluster into 141 galaxies.  Resampling GALAXIES gives +-0.343.  So '2.9 sigma from 1/2 and 7.2 sigma
  from 0' becomes 1.0 sigma from 1/2 and 2.4 sigma from 0 -- the kernel-family
  discrimination the candidate rests on does not reach 3 sigma once the errors are honest.
  ==> CANDIDATE K2 IS NOT A SECOND LAW.  It is a correct and pretty rewriting of the Route A kernel.
      Its one empirical statement is already decided in the literature, it carries no a_0 coefficient,
      and the measurement is limited by Upsilon and by the choice of estimator rather than by the data.

